entries.content:
Fixes a flying video sitting at 300x150 while its box animated around it, then jumping when metadata arrived.

- `MediaSurface` now gives the `VideoView` explicit `width`/`height` alongside `absoluteFill`. A DOM `<video>` is a REPLACED element: `position:absolute; inset:0` with `width/height:auto` resolves it to its INTRINSIC size (300x150 before metadata) rather than stretching it. The poster escaped this only because expo-image sizes its own element.
- New: `provideExpoVideo(module)`. On an ESM web bundler `typeof require` is `undefined`, so the optional-peer require cannot run and video degrades to its poster even when expo-video IS installed. Metro is unaffected. Call it once at startup on Vite:

      import * as ExpoVideo from "expo-video";
      provideExpoVideo(ExpoVideo);

Also adds browser gate phases for the video arm, the idle layer, paint latency and the no-origin flight.
